---
/**
 * /about/ — who the agency is, and whose network it belongs to.
 *
 * Section 4 of the brief asks for three things here: quiénes somos, liderazgo
 * and pertenencia a Omnicom. The third is the one that does SEO work, because
 * it is what declares the entity and its ownership chain, and section 2 lists
 * "sin JSON-LD: cero entidad declarada, sin cadena de propiedad Omnicom" among
 * the findings.
 *
 * WHERE THE CONTENT COMES FROM
 *   Nothing here is written from imagination. The current site has no about
 *   page at all, and the two sections on its home that look like one —
 *   "Proceso BBDO_" and "Nuestros Servicios_" — are lorem ipsum in production.
 *
 *   So: the leadership names and roles are the agency's own roster, the same
 *   data /people/ runs on. The network recognitions are BBDO Worldwide's, read
 *   off bbdo.com and labelled as the network's. The facts about how the agency
 *   works come from the Expansión article the agency itself republished, and
 *   are stated as reported rather than as slogans.
 *
 *   What is NOT here is a brand manifesto. The global has one and it is very
 *   good, and it is theirs. Ours has to be written by the creative director,
 *   and a placeholder in its place would only get shipped by accident.
 *
 * PENDING, and flagged rather than guessed:
 *   - Camilo Plazas is CEO according to the November 2024 article and the
 *     JSON-LD block drafted in the proposal, but he does NOT appear anywhere
 *     in the 117-person roster the current site publishes. Either he has left
 *     or BBDOers does not list him. The page therefore makes no claim about
 *     who runs the agency; it lists the leadership the roster does confirm.
 *   - Razón social, foundingDate and the new-business address are the same
 *     open questions the JSON-LD file carries.
 */
import { getCollection } from 'astro:content';
import { Image } from 'astro:assets';
import Base from '../layouts/Base.astro';
import ScrollFX from '../components/ScrollFX.astro';
import { NETWORK_RECOGNITIONS } from '../awards';
import { classify } from '../departments';
import { portraitOf } from '../portraits';

const everyone = await getCollection('people');

/**
 * classify() and not a copy of the leadership regex. The earlier version read
 * the pattern out of DEPARTMENTS and tested it directly, with a comment
 * claiming the two pages could not disagree. They only agreed because
 * 'liderazgo' happens to sit first in the array: classify() returns the FIRST
 * band that matches, so reordering it would have banded "Director General
 * Creativo" as Creatividad on /people/ while /about/ still called them
 * leadership. Going through the same function makes the claim true.
 */
const leadership = everyone
  .filter((person) => classify(person.data.role).id === 'liderazgo')
  .sort((a, b) => a.data.order - b.data.order || a.data.name.localeCompare(b.data.name, 'es'));

/** Counted, never typed. A hard-coded headcount goes stale the first hire. */
const headcount = everyone.length;
---

<Base
  title="Nosotros"
  path="/about/"
  description={`BBDO México es parte de BBDO Worldwide, red creativa de Omnicom Group. ${headcount} BBDOers en Ciudad de México.`}
>
  <ScrollFX />

  <main id="content">
    <header class="section-shell section-shell--head">
      {
        /* The spaces are deliberate. data-fx="lines" makes each child a block,
          so they stack whether or not there is whitespace between them — but
          without it the accessible name and the indexed text both come out as
          "SomosBBDOMéxico", one word. The same trap the headline hit with
          "BIGTHINGS". */
      }
      <h1 class="hero" data-fx="lines">
        <span>Somos </span>
        <span>BBDO </span>
        <span>México</span>
      </h1>
      <p class="lede" data-fx="up" data-fx-delay="120">
        Una agencia de {headcount} personas en Ciudad de México, parte de BBDO Worldwide y del grupo Omnicom.
      </p>
    </header>

    <section class="section-shell" aria-labelledby="who">
      <header class="section-head">
        <h2 id="who" data-fx="up">Cómo trabajamos</h2>
      </header>

      <div class="prose" data-fx="up">
        <p>
          La agencia reorganizó su forma de trabajar para dejar de responder únicamente a lo que
          pide un brief y anticiparse a lo que el cliente todavía no ha pedido. Sumó perfiles
          creativos con formación digital y de otras disciplinas, integró un departamento de Data y
          juntó a los equipos para que las ideas se trabajen entre áreas y no en serie.
        </p>
        <p>
          El equipo mezcla talento mexicano con profesionales de Venezuela, Chile, Colombia y
          Argentina, y eso se nota en campañas que funcionan en varios mercados de América Latina y
          no solo en México.
        </p>
      </div>
    </section>

    <section class="section-shell" aria-labelledby="leadership">
      <header class="section-head">
        <h2 id="leadership" data-fx="up">Liderazgo</h2>
        <a class="section-link" href="/people/">Conoce a los {headcount} BBDOers</a>
      </header>

      <ul class="leaders" data-fx-stagger>
        {
          leadership.map(async (person) => {
            const img = (await portraitOf(person.data.photo)).default;
            return (
              <li class="leader">
                <Image
                  class="leader__photo"
                  src={img}
                  alt={`Retrato de ${person.data.name}`}
                  widths={[240, 480]}
                  sizes="(min-width: 64rem) 240px, 45vw"
                  loading="lazy"
                  decoding="async"
                />
                <p class="leader__name">{person.data.name}</p>
                <p class="leader__role">{person.data.role}</p>
              </li>
            );
          })
        }
      </ul>
    </section>

    <section class="network" aria-labelledby="network">
      <div class="section-shell">
        <header class="section-head section-head--dark">
          <h2 id="network" data-fx="up">La red</h2>
        </header>

        <ol class="chain" data-fx-stagger>
          <li><span>BBDO México</span><small>Ciudad de México</small></li>
          <li><span>BBDO Worldwide</span><small>Red creativa global</small></li>
          <li><span>Omnicom Group</span><small>NYSE: OMC</small></li>
        </ol>

        <h3 class="network__title" data-fx="up">Reconocimientos de BBDO Worldwide</h3>
        <ul class="recognitions" data-fx-stagger>
          {
            NETWORK_RECOGNITIONS.map((item) => (
              <li>
                <span class="recognitions__name">{item.name}</span>
                <span class="recognitions__org">{item.org}</span>
                <span class="recognitions__years">{item.years.join(' · ')}</span>
              </li>
            ))
          }
        </ul>
        <p class="network__note">
          Estos reconocimientos son de la red BBDO Worldwide, no de la oficina de México.
        </p>
      </div>
    </section>
  </main>
</Base>

<style>
  .hero {
    font-family: var(--font-display);
    font-weight: var(--weight-display);
    text-transform: uppercase;
    font-size: clamp(2.5rem, 11vw, 7rem);
    line-height: var(--lh-display);
    margin: 0;
  }
  .lede {
    margin: var(--space-m) 0 0;
    font-size: 1.2rem;
    color: var(--color-dim);
    max-width: 44ch;
  }

  .prose p {
    max-width: 62ch;
    line-height: 1.6;
    margin: 0 0 var(--space-m);
  }

  /* --- Liderazgo ----------------------------------------------------------- */
  /* Fixed columns, not auto-fill: auto-fill packed seven tracks across a 90rem
     container and left each portrait 144px wide with a stranded last row. Five
     is the ceiling here — a face has to be recognisable for a leadership grid
     to do anything at all. */
  .leaders {
    list-style: none;
    margin: 0;
    padding: 0;
    display: grid;
    grid-template-columns: repeat(2, 1fr);
    gap: var(--space-l) var(--space-m);
  }
  .leader__photo {
    width: 100%;
    height: auto;
    aspect-ratio: 4 / 5;
    object-fit: cover;
    display: block;
  }
  .leader__name {
    margin: var(--space-xs) 0 0;
    font-family: var(--font-display);
    line-height: 1.15;
  }
  .leader__role {
    margin: 2px 0 0;
    font-size: 0.85rem;
    color: var(--color-dim);
  }

  /* --- La red -------------------------------------------------------------- */
  .network {
    background: var(--color-dark);
    color: var(--color-on-dark);
  }

  /* The chain reads downwards on a phone and across on a desktop, because it
     is an ownership chain and the direction is the information. */
  .chain {
    list-style: none;
    margin: 0 0 var(--space-2xl);
    padding: 0;
    display: grid;
    gap: var(--space-s);
  }
  .chain li {
    display: flex;
    flex-direction: column;
    padding-left: var(--space-m);
    border-left: 2px solid var(--color-red);
  }
  .chain span {
    font-family: var(--font-display);
    font-weight: var(--weight-display);
    font-size: clamp(1.25rem, 4vw, 2rem);
    text-transform: uppercase;
    line-height: 1.1;
  }
  .chain small {
    font-size: 0.85rem;
    color: rgb(250 250 250 / 60%);
  }

  .network__title {
    font-family: var(--font-display);
    text-transform: uppercase;
    letter-spacing: 0.08em;
    font-size: 0.9rem;
    margin: 0 0 var(--space-m);
    color: rgb(250 250 250 / 70%);
  }

  .recognitions {
    list-style: none;
    margin: 0;
    padding: 0;
    border-top: 1px solid rgb(250 250 250 / 18%);
  }
  .recognitions li {
    display: grid;
    gap: 2px;
    padding-block: var(--space-s);
    border-bottom: 1px solid rgb(250 250 250 / 18%);
  }
  .recognitions__name {
    font-family: var(--font-display);
    font-size: 1.05rem;
  }
  .recognitions__org {
    font-size: 0.85rem;
    color: var(--color-red);
  }
  .recognitions__years {
    font-size: 0.8rem;
    color: rgb(250 250 250 / 60%);
  }

  .network__note {
    margin: var(--space-m) 0 0;
    font-size: 0.85rem;
    color: rgb(250 250 250 / 60%);
    max-width: 52ch;
  }

  @media (min-width: 40rem) {
    .leaders {
      grid-template-columns: repeat(3, 1fr);
    }
  }
  @media (min-width: 64rem) {
    .leaders {
      grid-template-columns: repeat(5, 1fr);
    }
  }

  @media (min-width: 48rem) {
    .chain {
      grid-template-columns: repeat(3, 1fr);
    }
    .recognitions li {
      grid-template-columns: 2fr 1fr 1.4fr;
      align-items: baseline;
      gap: var(--space-m);
    }
  }
</style>
